  "solution": {
    "text": "Chlorotris(triphenylphosphine)rhodium(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>) is known as Wilkinson&#39;s catalyst. It is used as a homogeneous hydrogenation catalyst. It is a square planar <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>-</mo></math>electron complex. The oxidation state of Rhodium in it is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.",
